==Battleground==
*1 [[Master A.]] spawns as the boss after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Wafer Cat XL (Enemy)|Wafer Cat XL]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 66.67~73.33 seconds<sup>2,000f~2,200f</sup>.
*6 [[Gummy Cat (Enemy)|Gummy Cats]] spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.
*2 [[Chocolate Doge]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 80~86.67 seconds<sup>2,400f~2,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is somewhat odd, as the enemies use Gummy Cat to try and stop you from getting in range of hitting Master A. The Chocolate Doges aren't too big of a threat, but their [[Wave Attack#Mini-Waves|Mini-Waves]] and high HP can make them a little annoying. Thankfully unlike the original [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 9|Floor 9]], there are no [[Assassin Bear]]s to worry about, so there's no real reason to worry about stalling. You can use the enemies to use [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]] or [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attacks]] to snipe Master A. without much worry, and they don't push too hard.

